It's even worse:  Xorns can be generated 'out of area', 
in the 'ring' surrounding the play field.  Hence, 
digging out the level and filling it with brown puddings 
will not prevent Xorn generation.  A Xorn with a wand 
could hence be a show-stopper.  

Question:  At what minimum distance do monsters zap 
wands?  If this minimum distance is <8, I think you can 
just stay on the playground equator; else one would need 
at least three boulders to hide from Xorns on one side 
of the map.  That would mean an arragement like following: 

       PPPPP
       PP@PP
       P```P
       PPPPP
/////////////////

(the '/' shall indicate the end of playing field).  
Then you have 14 squares distance to the upper 
end of area, which should be enough, and the Xorns 
on the lower 'out of area' boundary can neither zap 
you[1] nor fool around with the boulders.  I assume that 
Xorns have infravision, hence it would not suffice to 
choose a dark place to hide...  

